---
const appropriateUses = [
  "Make important information easier to find and navigate.",
  "Offer simpler first explanations of complex material for human review.",
  "Support multilingual communication while preserving context and meaning.",
  "Organise educational knowledge, documents and recurring guidance.",
  "Reduce repetitive administrative work that takes time away from people.",
  "Help learners locate relevant material without pretending to replace teaching.",
  "Give teachers and academy teams a structured first draft to check and improve.",
];

const safeguards = [
  {
    title: "Accuracy",
    text: "AI can produce incomplete, outdated or incorrect answers. Important educational information must be checked.",
  },
  {
    title: "Human judgment",
    text: "Educators, learners and responsible decision-makers remain essential—especially where context or consequences matter.",
  },
  {
    title: "Privacy",
    text: "Personal or sensitive learner information should not be collected or shared without a clear, justified and protected process.",
  },
  {
    title: "Honest boundaries",
    text: "AI must not diagnose learning, medical or psychological conditions, guarantee examination success or invent institutional facts.",
  },
  {
    title: "Proportion",
    text: "The simplest effective approach may not require AI. Complexity is justified only when it creates clear educational value.",
  },
];
---

<section class="responsible-ai section" id="responsible-ai" aria-labelledby="responsible-ai-title">
  <div class="container">
    <header class="responsible-ai__header">
      <div class="flow">
        <p class="eyebrow">Responsible AI in education</p>
        <h2 id="responsible-ai-title">AI should support learning—not replace understanding.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="lede">
        AI can be useful when it improves access, clarity or routine support. It should not replace educators,
        human judgment, learner effort or responsibility for important decisions.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="responsible-ai__balance">
      <section class="ai-support" aria-labelledby="ai-support-title">
        <div class="ai-panel-heading">
          <span aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">Where it may help</p>
            <h3 id="ai-support-title">Useful support with a clear purpose</h3>
          </div>
        </div>
        <ul>
          {appropriateUses.map((item) => (
            <li>
              <svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 20 20" width="20" height="20">
                <path d="m4 10 3.5 3.5L16 5.8" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" />
              </svg>
              <span>{item}</span>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="ai-safeguards" aria-labelledby="ai-safeguards-title">
        <div class="ai-panel-heading">
          <span aria-hidden="true">!</span>
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">What must remain protected</p>
            <h3 id="ai-safeguards-title">Clear limits and human responsibility</h3>
          </div>
        </div>
        <dl>
          {safeguards.map((item) => (
            <div>
              <dt>{item.title}</dt>
              <dd>{item.text}</dd>
            </div>
          ))}
        </dl>
      </section>
    </div>

    <aside class="ai-decision-gate" aria-labelledby="ai-gate-title">
      <header>
        <p class="eyebrow">Before AI enters the solution</p>
        <h3 id="ai-gate-title">Four questions come first.</h3>
      </header>
      <ol>
        <li><span>01</span><p>What educational problem needs to improve?</p></li>
        <li><span>02</span><p>Would a simpler approach solve it well?</p></li>
        <li><span>03</span><p>What information, privacy and accuracy risks exist?</p></li>
        <li><span>04</span><p>Where will human review and responsibility remain?</p></li>
      </ol>
      <p class="ai-decision-gate__outcome">
        <strong>AI is not the starting point.</strong>
        A useful, safe and understandable educational outcome is.
      </p>
    </aside>
  </div>
</section>
